# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# assessment-models.github.io — ignore rules
#
# STANDING RULE: this repository is PUBLIC and is served to the world at
# https://assessment-models.github.io/. Machine-local scratch state must never
# be published here. The rules below are the repo's own guard: the repository
# refuses these paths on its own, so no operator, bot or agent can commit them
# by oversight.
#
# These rules are a guard against ACCIDENTAL publication, not a security
# control. A deliberate `git add -f` still overrides them. That is the
# intended escape hatch for genuinely shared project configuration — it must
# be used consciously, never by accident.
#
# Keep this file ordered by class. Do not add a rule that would match an
# already-tracked file: that is how a tracked file silently stops being
# published.
#
# NOTE: gitignore has NO inline-comment syntax. A trailing "# ..." on a rule
# line becomes part of the pattern and silently stops matching. Put the
# explanation on its own line above the rule.
#
# ENFORCED IN CI: scripts/verify-no-local-residue.mjs checks the tracked tree
# against this same list and fails if any rule below has gone missing. That
# check is the load-bearing guard, because an archive extracted over this
# repository root can carry its own .gitignore and overwrite this file,
# silently dropping every rule here — at which point the residue becomes
# committable again with no visible signal. The tracked-tree check holds
# regardless of what this file currently says.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Local authoring-tool scratch state -------------------------------------
# Never publish. Machine-local workspaces of authoring / agent tools: session
# artifacts, scratch media, tool-local caches. Observed residue in the
# 2026-11-21 site archive: .aistudio/artifacts/brain/<uuid>/.tempmediaStorage/
# (13 PNG/WEBM files, 3.2 MB) — unreferenced by any site source.
.aistudio/
.tempmediaStorage/
.cursor/
.claude/
.gemini/
.codex/
.aider*
.continue/

# --- Lockfiles for package managers this repo does not use -------------------
# The deploy toolchain is npm only (.github/workflows/deploy.yml runs `npm ci`),
# so package-lock.json is tracked and authoritative. Any other manager's
# lockfile is residue from a different local toolchain and carries no
# dependency information this build can use.
bun.lock
bun.lockb
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# --- Editor and OS scratch --------------------------------------------------
# Local editor / OS droppings. Never part of site content.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.Spotlight-V100/
.Trashes/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.\#*
\#*\#

# --- Language runtime scratch -----------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode caches from running scripts/sync_org_catalog.py locally.
# Never repository content.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Patch and merge residue ------------------------------------------------
# Leftovers from an interrupted rebase, a conflicted apply, or a patch run.
# They are transient by definition and must not enter the history.
*.orig
*.rej

# --- Credential-bearing files -----------------------------------------------
# This repository is public. Credentials belong in CI secrets, never in a
# tracked file. Only *.example templates are exempt, so a template can still
# be committed while the real thing never can.
.env
.env.*
!.env*.example

# --- Logs and CI scratch ----------------------------------------------------
# Logs are never site content. Safe to ignore: the catalog sync workflow
# writes sync-output.log with `tee` and reads it back from the working tree —
# gitignore does not affect file existence — and it commits only the two
# registry JSON files by explicit path.
*.log
diag-lines.txt

# --- Build output and dependency trees --------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
.tmp/
public/models.json
public/snapshot/
